name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I would lean towards the solution proposed by the SIG: only support configurability when users explicitly request it. After all, enabling configurability after `RemoveAll()` is an operation that ensures both extensibility compatibility and backward compatibility.\\n\\n@akats7 @dmathieu \\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T02:01:52Z\\n\\nAh gotcha, didn't see that that was mentioned. I'm good on holding off until it's explicitly requested.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T04:27:26Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J I think we're good to resolve the conflicts and close this out, thanks!\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T11:58:48Z\\n\\nI’ve resolved the conflicts, and the otelgin package tests passed on my machine @flc1125 @dmathieu @akats7 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T14:02:53Z\\n\\nCould you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T15:21:14Z\\n\\n> Could you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> \\n\\n> > My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nI’ve added more details to the test case, it now includes two extra middlewares, one upstream and one downstream, to demonstrate what happens when `RemoveAll` is called in the otel middleware. The behavior is correct to me, but let’s confirm that we all agree it’s the expected one.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i would lean toward the solut propos by the sig onli support configur when user explicit request it after all enabl configur after removeal is an oper that ensur both extens compat and backward compat akats7 dmathieu akats7 2025 11 10t02 01 52z ah gotcha didn t see that that wa mention i m good on hold off until it s explicit request akats7 2025 11 10t04 27 26z yile j i think we re good to resolv the conflict and close this out thank yile j 2025 11 10t11 58 48z i ve resolv the conflict and the otelgin packag test pass on my machin flc1125 dmathieu akats7 flc1125 2025 11 10t14 02 53z could you add the correspond unit test for this scenario my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data yile j 2025 11 10t15 21 14z could you add the correspond unit test for this scenario my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data i ve ad more detail to the test case it now includ two extra middlewar one upstream and one downstream to demonstr what happen when removeal is call in the otel middlewar the behavior is correct to me but let s confirm that we all agre it s the expect one sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"8a1254612e6e6337\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2961419723879307, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11683721483990109, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71451974, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"issue 5946 marked duplicate 2025-07-02 reason duplicate resolution otelgin multipart form\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
